  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2227$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $7$ is prime or divisible by $10.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{7\\text{\u00a0is prime}}_{\u23df}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{7\\text{\u00a0is divisible by\u00a0}10}_{\u23df}}_{D}\n$$\n\nthat is, $P\u2228D.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $5$ is rational or less than $100.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{5\\text{\u00a0is rational}}_{\u23df}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{5\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}100}_{\u23df}}_{L},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q\u2228L.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{7\\text{\u00a0is prime\u00a0}\\text{or}\\text{\u00a0divisible by\u00a0}10}_{\u23df}}_{P\\,\u2228\\,D}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{5\\text{\u00a0is rational\u00a0}\\text{or}\\text{\u00a0less than\u00a0}100}_{\u23df}}_{Q\\,\u2228\\,L},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P\u2228D)\u2227(Q\u2228L).$",
